      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change looks ok by tracing the code, but it would be nice to have a functional test of some sort to ensure purge_mappings is doing what it should for both `user` and `group` types.\n\nThis test case wouldn\u0027t necessarily catch the bug if it were reintroduced, because the issue was the \u0027type\u0027 was getting set in the purge_filter instead of \u0027entity_type\u0027. This resulted in all of the mappings getting purged since the query wasn\u0027t being built properly. Maybe was we can do is:\n\n - create an id mapping for a group\n - create an id mapping for a user\n - perform a mapping purge using the cli.py module with --type user\n - ensure the public id of the user is gone\n - ensure the public id for the group still exists\n\nWe could reverse that test case for group logic, too.",
